# ISO/IEC 27001:2022 GAP ANALYSIS & AUDIT REPORT
**Target Organization:** CloudVault Tech Inc.
**Auditor:** Lead GRC Analyst
**Framework:** ISO/IEC 27001:2022 Annex A Controls
**Assessment Date:** August 12, 2026

---

## 1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
A pre-certification Gap Analysis was conducted for CloudVault Tech Inc. to evaluate operational readiness for ISO/IEC 27001:2022 certification. The assessment evaluated controls across Organizational, People, Physical, and Technological domains.

The audit identified **3 major compliance gaps** that will result in Non-Conformities (NCs) during an official certification audit if left unaddressed.

---

## 2. ISO 27001:2022 CONTROL GAP MATRIX

| ISO Control ID | Control Name | Domain | Current Operational State | Compliance Status | Remediation Required |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Control A.8.20** | Network Security | Technological | Staff work on public Wi-Fi without VPN/encryption enforcement. | **NON-COMPLIANT** | Enforce mandatory VPN with AES-256 split-tunneling on all managed laptops. |
| **Control A.6.1** | Screening | People | Background checks completed 3 weeks post-hire date. | **NON-COMPLIANT** | Mandate pre-employment screening clearance prior to issuing Active Directory credentials. |
| **Control A.8.13** | Information Backup | Technological | Database backups executing daily, but restoration testing unperformed for >12 months. | **NON-COMPLIANT** | Establish quarterly automated backup restoration test drills with logged integrity checks. |

